  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Acts as a negative regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway by promoting the degradation of beta-catenin. Down-regulates beta-catenin by acting as a scaffold protein for the beta-catenin destruction complex, which phosphorylates beta-catenin, leading to its ubiquitination and degradation. AXIN2 probably facilitates the phosphorylation of CTNNB1 and APC by GSK3B. Itself is a transcriptional target of the Wnt/beta-catenin pathway, creating a negative feedback loop. When constitutively localized to the nucleus, alters the chromatin structure at the MYC promoter and directly represses MYC gene expression.",
    "catalytic_activity": null,
    "subcellular_location": ["Cytoplasm", "Nucleus", "Mitotic spindle", "Beta-catenin destruction complex"],
    "tissue_specificity": "Ubiquitous expression with low tissue specificity (Tau=0.30). Expression enhanced in colorectal cancer due to Wnt pathway activation. Medium expression in hepatocytes and low brain regional specificity.",
