    "pathway_role_summary": "AXIN2 is a scaffold protein in the beta-catenin destruction complex, coordinating GSK3B and CK1A1 kinases to phosphorylate beta-catenin for proteasomal degradation. It serves as a negative regulator of Wnt signaling and is itself a transcriptional target of the pathway, creating a negative feedback loop. AXIN2 turnover is regulated by tankyrase-mediated PARsylation followed by RNF146 ubiquitination, and by SIAH1-mediated ubiquitination."
  },
