    "data_quality_notes": "High-quality data with multiple crystal structures for individual domains (RGS, DIX, beta-catenin binding). Some PTM sites (especially phosphorylation) differ between AXIN1 and AXIN2 - CK1α phosphorylation site conserved in AXIN1 but not AXIN2. Kinetic data limited to binding affinities (Kd values) for tankyrase and GSK3B; catalytic parameters (Kcat, Km) not extensively reported. Most interaction studies do not distinguish between AXIN1 and AXIN2. Isoform 2 sequence not fully characterized.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "AXIN2 is a critical scaffold in Wnt signaling with well-defined binding sites for multiple partners. Key for modeling: (1) Sequential phosphorylation mechanism - CK1A1 primes beta-catenin followed by GSK3B; (2) Negative feedback loop - AXIN2 expression induced by Wnt pathway it inhibits; (3) Degradation regulation via tankyrase-RNF146 and SIAH1 pathways; (4) Phase separation and polymerization via DIX domain affects activity; (5) Nuclear-cytoplasmic shuttling adds spatial regulation. Quantitative binding data available for tankyrase (Kd ~1-5 μM) and GSK3B (Kd ~3 μM). AXIN2 shows non-redundant functions compared to AXIN1 in destruction complex formation."
  }
